hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5711","I have forgiven so-and-so and have nullified your deeds."
"5712","The old man said: O Yamami, come forward. Never say to anyone, ""May Allah not forgive you."" By Allah, Allah will never admit you to Paradise. I asked, ""Who are you? May Allah have mercy on you."" He replied: ""I am Abu Hurairah."" I said: ""Such words are sometimes used by one of us for his wife or servant when he expresses anger at them."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Do not say this, because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Among the Children of Israel there were two men who were brothers to each other. One of them was devoted to worship and the other was a sinner. The worshipper saw the sinner committing a sin and said to him: 'Reduce this.' The other man replied: 'Leave this matter between me and my Lord.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worshipper repeated his words to him, and the other man gave the same reply: 'Leave me and my Lord.' Until one day, the worshipper saw him committing a sin and considered his sin to be great. He said: 'Woe to you! Refrain from sinning.' The other man said: 'Leave me and my Lord. Were you sent as a watcher over me?' The worshipper said: 'By Allah, Allah will never forgive you.' (The narrator is unsure, perhaps these were the words.) Or he said: 'Allah will never admit you to Paradise.' (The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) Then an angel was sent to both of them, who took their souls. They both appeared before Allah, the Exalted. The Lord asked the worshipper: 'Are you a scholar, or do you have power over what is in My control, or do you prevent My mercy from reaching My servant?' (Then He said to the sinner:) 'Go to Paradise.' (The narrator says: That is, Allah said this to the sinful person.) And to the other He said: 'Take him to Hell.' (The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or perhaps Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said:) 'By Him in Whose hand is my soul, he uttered a word that destroyed his world and his Hereafter.'"
"5713","None of you should say: Woe be upon the Time, for verily Allah is the Time. (Using translation from Muslim 2246d)"
"5716","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A person says something to make his companions laugh, but because of it he will fall deeper (into Hell) than the distance between the earth and the star Thurayya (Pleiades, which is very high)."
"5717","The narrator named Wahb says: That is, it is in his tongue."
"5718","narrates: Two men who had come from the east stood up to deliver a sermon. Both of them spoke, then they both sat down. Then Sayyiduna Thabit bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him), who was the orator of the Prophet (peace be upon him), stood up. He spoke, and the people liked his speech. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up and delivered a sermon. He (peace be upon him) said: O people! Speak according to common usage, for making speech lengthy and embellished is from Satan, and some eloquence is (like) magic."
"5719","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Indeed, Allah the Exalted has disliked three things for you: pointless argumentation, wasting wealth, and asking (or begging) excessively.” Ibn ‘Ulayyah says: Wasting wealth means spending it unjustly."",""Ibn 'Ulayyah said"",""""""Wasting wealth is spending it in an unjust manner."""""""
"5720","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah the Exalted has disliked for you idle disputation, excessive questioning (or asking), and wasting wealth."
"5721","“The stronger believer is better and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, although both are good. Strive to seek that which will benefit you and do not feel helpless. If something overwhelms you, then say: Qaddarallah, wa ma sha'a fa’al (It is the decree of Allah and what He wills He does). And beware of (saying) ‘If only,’ for ‘If only’ opens the door to Satan.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4168)"
"5722","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, although both are good. Strive for that which will benefit you, seek the help of Allah, and do not feel helpless. If anything befalls you, do not say, ""if only I had done such and such"" rather say ""Qaddara Allahu wa ma sha'a fa'ala (Allah has decreed and whatever he wills, He does)."" For (saying) 'If' opens (the door) to the deeds of Satan.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 79)"
"5723","I have created crops,' rather he should say: 'I have cultivated the land.'"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Have you not heard the statement of Allah Almighty: ""What is your opinion, have you cultivated it, or are We the ones who cause it to grow?"
"5724","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""None of you should say Khabuthat Nafsi, but he is recommended to say 'Laqisat Nafsi."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6179)"
"5725","I used to hear these words from your tongues before, and you used to hurt me through them. Now do not say: 'What Allah willed and what Muhammad (peace be upon him) willed.'"
"5726","Sayyiduna Iyad bin Himar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I submitted, \""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), a person from my tribe abuses me. He is of a lower status than me. Should I take revenge on him?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Both individuals who abuse each other are two devils. They quarrel and they lie.\"""""
"5727","Sayyiduna Iyad bin Himar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said, \""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! A man from my tribe insults me, and he is of lesser status than me. Will I be sinful if I take revenge on him?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Two people who insult each other are both devils; both of them escalate the matter and speak falsely.\""(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used t"
"5728","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whatever two people who insult each other say: its burden is upon the one who started it, as long as the oppressed does not exceed the limits."
"5729","When two persons indulge in hurling (abuses) upon one another, it would be the first one who would be the sinner so long as the oppressed does not transgress the limits. (Using translation from Muslim 2587)"
"5730","When a man who had drunk wine was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: Beat him. Abu Hurairah said: Some struck him with their hands, some with their garment. When he turned his face, some people said: Allah put you shame! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not say like that and help the devil to get power over him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4477)"
"5731","The Prophet ﷺ said: Do not curse the cock, for it awakens for prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5101)"
"5732","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The wind comes from Allah's mercy. Salamah's version has: It is Allah's mercy; it (sometimes) brings blessing and (sometimes) brings punishment. So when you see it, do not revile it, but ask Allah for some of its good, and seek refuge in Allah from its evil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5097)"
"5733","""One who brings peace between people is not a liar, he says something good, or reports something good."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1938)"
"5734","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""You must be truthful, for it leads to righteousness and they are both in Paradise. And beware of dishonesty, for it leads to wickedness and they are both in the Hellfire."" (Using translation from Ṭabarānī 17005)"
"5735","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Beware! Indeed, lying blackens the face and tale-bearing is a cause of punishment in the grave."
"5736","""There was no behavior more hated to the Messenger of Allah than lying. A man would lie in narrating something in the presence of the Prophet, and he would not be content until he knew that he had repented."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1973)"
"5737","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) says: Once, he passed by a tyrant ruler, and with Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was his wife, Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her). The king was informed that there is a man here accompanied by a very beautiful woman. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) says: That man summoned Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) went to him, and when he was questioned, Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) said: ""She is my (religious) sister."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) says: Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) came to Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) and told her that the ruler had asked about her, and he had told him: ""You are my sister, so in the Book of Allah you are my sister, so do not consider me a liar."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) says: When the ruler saw Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her), he approached her. Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) prayed for harm against him, so he was seized. The man said: ""Pray to Allah for me; I promise I will not repeat this mistake."" Then Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) prayed for him, and he again tried to approach her. Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) again prayed against him, and he was seized again, more severely than before. He said: ""Pray to Allah for me; I promise I will not do this again."" Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) prayed for him again, and he again tried to approach her. Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) again prayed for harm, and he was seized again, more severely than the previous two times. He said: ""Pray to Allah for me; I promise I will not do this again."" Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) prayed for him, and he was cured. He said to his minister: ""You did not bring a human to me; you brought a devil to me."" Then he gave Sayyidah Hajarah (may Allah be pleased with her) as a servant to Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her). When Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) saw this woman, he asked: ""Where did she come from?"" Sayyidah Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: ""Allah Almighty foiled the plot of the disbelieving sinner and gave Hajarah (may Allah be pleased with her) as a servant."" Whenever Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith, he would also say: ""O people who are nourished by heavenly water, she is your mother."" The narrator named Nadr would say these words in a loud voice. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The term ""nourished by heavenly water"" is used for the children of Sayyidah Hajarah (may Allah be pleased with her) because Sayyiduna Isma'il (peace be upon him) was the son of Sayyidah Hajarah (may Allah be pleased with her), and his upbringing was through the water of Zamzam, which is heavenly water. Through this, Allah Almighty honored Sayyiduna Isma'il (peace be upon him). At the time when his mother, Sayyidah Hajarah (may Allah be pleased with her), gave birth to him, his descendants are those who were nourished by heavenly water."
"5738","I have a co-wife. Is there any harm for me if I give her the false impression (of getting something from my husband which he has not in fact given me)? Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The one who creates such a (false impression) of receiving what one has not been given is like one who wears the garment of falsehood. (Using translation from Muslim 2130a)"
"5739","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: A person who pretends to be satisfied with something that was not given to him is like one who wears two garments of falsehood."
"5740","The narrator says: The people did exactly that. The sight of that she-camel is as if still before my eyes; it was an ashen-colored she-camel. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The uncle of the narrator Abu Qilabah is Amr bin Mu’awiyah bin Zayd al-Jarmi, whose kunyah is Abu Muhallab. Imam Awza’i was mistaken about his kunyah, so he said: His kunyah is Abu Muhajir. The reason is that even a rider sometimes stumbles."
"5741","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Leave this mount, for it has been cursed."" The narrator states that the luggage was then unloaded from that mount. Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The sight of that she-camel is as if still before my eyes; it was an ash-colored she-camel."
"5742","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired, ""Who is the one who cursed his camel?"" That man replied, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! It is I."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Get down from it. Do not keep a cursed one with us. Do not invoke curses upon yourselves, nor upon your possessions, for you do not know if it may coincide with a time in which the supplication is accepted for you."
"5743","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came to that mountain. When the girl saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), she began to say, “Get up! O Allah, curse him! O Allah, curse him!” The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: “No mount upon which there is Allah’s curse will remain with us.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The command of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) to abandon the mount upon which a curse was invoked contains a hidden ruling, which is the reason for it: that the supplication of the one who curses may be answered. So, when it is known that the supplication of the one who curses has been answered, then we will command him to abandon that mount. But due to the cessation of revelation, it is no longer possible to know this; therefore, it is not permissible for anyone to act upon this deed now."",""There was a servant girl between us"",""riding on a camel or a mule carrying the belongings of the people between two mountains. The mountain became tight for her"","" and then the Messenger of Allahﷺ came upon her. When she saw him"","" she started to say"","" 'May Allah curse him! O Allah"","" curse him!' The Messenger of Allahﷺ said"","" 'Do not accompany us on a mount that is cursed by Allah.'"""""""
"5744","I have seen that the majority of the inhabitants of Hell are you women. The women asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! What is the reason for this? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. O group of women, I have not seen any creature more deficient in intelligence and religion who can take away the sense of a wise and experienced man than you. The women asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! What is the deficiency in our intelligence and religion? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: Is not the testimony of a woman half that of a man? The women replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: This is due to the deficiency in her intelligence. When a woman menstruates, does she not leave off prayer and fasting? The women replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: This is the deficiency in her religion. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) turned from there and proceeded towards his house. The wife of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her), sought permission to enter upon the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). It was said in the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) wishes to enter. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Which Zainab? He (peace be upon him) was told: The wife of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Yes, let this woman enter. She was given permission to enter. She said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Today you have instructed us to give charity. I have some jewelry and I intended to give it in charity, but Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) thinks that he and his children are more deserving of it. Should I give this jewelry to them in charity? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: He has spoken the truth; your husband and your children are more deserving of it, so give it to them in charity."
"5745","""Do not curse the wind, for it is merely doing as ordered , and whoever curses something undeservingly, then the curse returns upon him."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1978)"
"5746","I heard Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, those who curse will neither be witnesses nor intercessors on the Day of Resurrection."
"5747","He heard the Prophet ﷺ, when he raised his head in the last rak'ah of the subh prayer, say: ""O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,"" supplicating against some of the hypocrites. Then Allah revealed the words: ""Not for you is the decision; whether He turns in mercy to (pardon) them or punishes them; verily, they are the wrongdoers."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1078)"
"5748","“May Allah curse the thief! He steals an egg and his hand is cut off, and he steals a rope and his hand is cut off” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2583)"
"5749",""" Six are cursed, being cursed by Allah and by every Prophet that came: The one who adds to Allah's Book, the one who denies Allah's Qadar, the one who rules with tyranny by which he honors whom Allah has debased, and he dishonors whom Allah has honored, and the one who legalizes what Allah forbade, and the one from my family who legalizes what Allah forbade, and the abandoner of my Sunnah."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2154)"
"5750","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed women who imitate men and men who imitate women."
"5751","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the man who dressed like a woman and the woman who dressed like a man. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4098)"
"5752","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the man who dressed like a woman and the woman who dressed like a man. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4098)"
"5753","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: In the last era, there will be some people who will ride saddles like men, they will resemble men, they will camp at the doors of mosques, their women will be clothed yet naked, on their heads will be humps like those of Bactrian camels (hair tied in the shape of humps). You should curse them because they are accursed. If there were any nation after you, then their women would serve them just as the women of previous nations served you."
"5754","The worst amongst the people is the double-faced one; he comes to some people with one face and to others with the other face. (Using translation from Muslim 2526c)"
"5755","The worst amongst the people is the double-faced one; he comes to some people with one face and to others with the other face. (Using translation from Muslim 2526c)"
"5756","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever is two-faced in this world, on the Day of Resurrection he will have two tongues made of fire."
"5757","You would find people like those of mine, the good amongst you in the Days of Ignorance would be good amongst you in the days of Islam, provided they have an understanding of it and you will find good amongst people the persons who would be averse to position of authority until it is thrust upon them, and you will find the worst amongst persons one who has double face. He comes with one face to them and with the other face to the others. (Using translation from Muslim 2526a)"
"5758","Do you know what is backbiting? They (the Companions) said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: Backbiting implies your talking about your brother in a manner which he does not like. It was said to him: What is your opinion about this that if I actually find (that failing) in my brother which I made a mention of? He said: If (that failing) is actually found (in him) what you assert, you in fact backbited him, and if that is not in him it is a slander. (Using translation from Muslim 2589)"
"5759","Do you know what is backbiting? They (the Companions) said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: Backbiting implies your talking about your brother in a manner which he does not like. It was said to him: What is your opinion about this that if I actually find (that failing) in my brother which I made a mention of? He said: If (that failing) is actually found (in him) what you assert, you in fact backbited him, and if that is not in him it is a slander. (Using translation from Muslim 2589)"
"5760","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “If you follow the faults of people, you will corrupt them or risk corrupting them.”"",""He said that Abū Dardāʾ said"",""“Muʿāwiyah heard ˹this˺ statement from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Allah benefited him by it.”"""
"5761","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “One of you may see a splinter in your brother's eye, but forget the log in your own.”"
"5762","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When you hear someone saying that people have perished, then that person himself will be the one most likely to perish among them."
"5763","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the Minbar and called out with a raised voice: ’O you who accepted Islam with his tongue, while faith has not reached his heart! Do not harm the Muslims, nor revile them, nor spy on them to expose their secrets. For indeed whoever tries to expose his Muslims brother’s secrets, Allah exposes his secrets wide open, even if he were in the depth of his house.’” He (Nafl’) said: ‘ One day Ibn ‘Umar looked at the House- or – the Ka’bah and said: ‘What is it that is more honored than you, and whose honor is more sacred than yours! And the believer’s honor is more sacred to Allah than yours.’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2032)"
"5764","a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, there is someone who is mentioned regarding her performing a lot of Ṣalāh, ˹keeping a lot of˺ of fasts, and giving ˹a lot˺ of charity, except that she harms her neighbors with her tongue."" He, ˹the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,˺ said, ""She is in the Hellfire."" ˹The man˺ said, ""O Messenger of Allah, ˹and˺ there is someone who is mentioned regarding her not performing much Ṣalāh, ˹and not keeping many˺ of fasts, and not giving ˹much˺ of charity, however, she gives the milk curds of her oxens as charity, and she does not harm her neighbors with her tongue."" He, ˹the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,˺ said, ""She is in Jannah."" (Using translation from Aḥmad 9675)"
"5765","The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise."
"5766","""A man praised another man in the presence of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Woe to you,you have cut the neck of your companion,'several times. Then he said: 'If anyone of you praises his brother, let him say: ""I think he is lie this, but I do not sanctify anyone before Allah."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3744)"
"5767","""A man praised another man in the presence of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Woe to you,you have cut the neck of your companion,'several times. Then he said: 'If anyone of you praises his brother, let him say: ""I think he is lie this, but I do not sanctify anyone before Allah."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3744)"
"5768","It was said to Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What is your opinion about the person who has done good deeds and the people praise him? He said: It is glad tidings for a believer (which he has received in this mortal world). (Using translation from Muslim 2642a)"
"5769","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Throw dust in the faces of those who excessively praise (others)."
"5770","A man came and praised ‘Uthman in his face, al-Miqdad b. Al-Aswad took dust and threw it on his face, saying : The Apostle of Allah ﷺ said : When you see those who are given to praising people, throw dust in their faces. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4804)"
"5771","I testify and state that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not turn his back. However, some hasty people among the people, when they came under the target of the arrows of the Hawazin tribe, (they retreated). At that time, Sayyiduna Abu Sufyan bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) was holding the reins of the white mule of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying: I am a Prophet, this is not a lie, I am the son of Abdul Muttalib."
"5772","I had blessings equal to the number of these branches, I would distribute them among you. You will not find me to be a liar or a coward.”"
"5773","If I were to see a man with my wife, I would have struck him with the sword, and not with the flat part (side) of it. When Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of that, he said: Are you surprised at Sa'd's jealousy of his honour? By Allah, I am more jealous of my honour than he, and Allah is more jealous than I. Because of His jealousy Allah has prohibited abomination, both open and secret And no person is more jealous of his honour than Allah, and no persons, is more fond of accepting an excuse than Allah, on account of which He has sent messengers, announcers of glad tidings and warners; and no one is more fond of praise than Allah on account of which Allah has promised Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 1499a)"
"5774","The Dajjal will come from that direction until he crosses the Uhud mountain, then the angels will turn him towards Syria, where he will meet his destruction."
"5775","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Do not boast about your ancestors from the time of ignorance. By the One in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad, for a man to have his nose filled with dust is better than for him to boast about those ancestors of his who died in the time of ignorance."
"5776","The honorable man who was the son of an honorable man, who was the son of an honorable man, who was the son of an honorable man is Sayyiduna Yusuf (Joseph), peace be upon him, who was the son of Sayyiduna Yaqub (Jacob), peace be upon him, who was the son of Sayyiduna Ishaq (Isaac), peace be upon him, who was the son of Sayyiduna Ibrahim (Abraham), peace be upon him. May Allah send blessings upon them."
"5777","""If a man were to fill his stomach completely with pus until it destroyed him, that would be better for him than filling (his mind) with poetry."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3760)"
"5778","In poetry there is wisdom. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5010)"
"5779","""If a man were to fill his stomach completely with pus until it destroyed him, that would be better for him than filling (his mind) with poetry."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3760)"
"5780","A desert Arab came to the Prophet ﷺ and began to speak. Thereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: In eloquence there is magic and in poetry there is wisdom. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5011)"
"5781","""I sat with the Prophet ﷺ more than one-hundred times. His Companions used to recite poetry and talk about things that occurred during Jahiliyyah, and he would remain silent, and sometimes he would smile along with them."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2850)"
"5782","I replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Recite it. I recited a verse to him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Recite more. I recited again to him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) kept saying to me: Recite more, until I had recited one hundred verses to him."
"5783","The best verse of poetry ever said by any Arab is this line of Labid: 'Beware! Everything except Allah Almighty is perishable.'"
"5784","The best verse of poetry ever said by any Arab is the saying of Labid: ""Beware! Everything except Allah Almighty is perishable."" (The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said:) Umayyah bin Abi al-Salt had come very close to accepting Islam."
"5785","""The worst of all people lying is a man who trades insults with another man, disparaging the entire tribe, and a man who denies his father and accuses his mother of adultery."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3761)"
"5786","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""A believer strives with his sword and with his tongue. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, you (by satirizing them) are as if you are striking them with spears."
"5787","Hassan bin Thabit asked the permission of Messenger of Allah ﷺ to lampoon the pagans (in verse). Allah's Apostle said, ""What about my fore-fathers (ancestry)?' Hassan said (to the Prophet) ""I will take you out of them as a hair is taken out of dough."" Narrated Hisham bin ʿUrwa that his father said, ""I called Hassan with bad names in front of ʿAisha."" She said, ""Don't call him with bad names because he used to defend Messenger of Allah ﷺ (against the pagans). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6150)"
"5788","I believe in Your command. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: O Ibn Rawahah! Are you reciting poetry in front of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: O Umar! Let him do it. These verses are more severe (painful) for them (the disbelievers) than being struck with spears."
"5789","narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Khandaq, the Ansar recited these verses: ""We are the people who have pledged allegiance to Muhammad (peace be upon him) that as long as we live, we will continue to strive (in jihad)."" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) replied to them by reciting this verse: ""True life is only the life of the Hereafter. (O Allah) honor the Ansar and the Muhajirin."
"5790","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Zahir is our villager and we are his townspeople."" The narrator states: Once, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came to him while he was (standing in the market) selling his goods. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) encircled him from behind with his arms. That man could not see you (the Prophet, peace be upon him). He said: ""Let me go, who is it?"" When he turned around and realized that it was the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), he pressed his back against the chest of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: ""Who will buy this slave?"" Zahir said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! You will find me of little value."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""But in the sight of Allah, you are not of little value (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), rather, in the sight of Allah, you are valuable."
"5791","I have made a covenant with my Lord that for any individual of my Ummah for whom I make a supplication of harm, and he is not deserving of it, then Allah will make that supplication a means of purification for him and a means of nearness to Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"5792","“If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4191)"
"5793","“If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4191)"
"5794",""" When the basest of them broke forth with mischief"" (xei. 12). When A mischievous person, strong even because of the strength of a family like Abu Zam'a, broke forth. He then delivered instruction in regard to the women saying: There is amongst you who beats his woman, and in the narration on the authority of Abu Bakr, the words are: He flogs her like a slave-girl. And in the narration of Abu Kuraib (the words are): He flogs like a slave and then comforts his bed with the help of that at the end of the day, and he then advised in regard to laughing of people at the breaking of wind and said: One of you laughs at that which you yourself do. (Using translation from Muslim 2855)"
"5795","When two men who came from the east made a speech and the people were charmed with their eloquence, the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) said: In some eloquent speech there is magic. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5007)"
"5796","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Eloquence is from Allah, and inability is from Satan. Eloquence does not mean excessive speech, rather eloquence means to distinguish between the truth. And inability does not mean speaking little, rather it is to act foolishly in matters of truth.”"
"5797","“People are like a hundred camels; you can hardly find one worth riding among them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3990)"
"5798","There was a feeling of fright in Medina, so the Prophet ﷺ borrowed a horse called Mandub belonging 'to Abu Talha and mounted it. (On his return), he said, ""I did not see anything of fright and I found this horse very fast."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2862)"
"5799","I said: By Allah, I will not give him permission until I seek permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding him. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! The brother of Abu Qais, Aflaḥ, sought permission to enter upon me, so I refused to give him permission until I seek your permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Why did you not give permission to your uncle to enter? Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! The man did not breastfeed me, his wife breastfed me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He is your uncle, you should have given him permission to enter, may your hands be dusted. Urwah narrates: For this reason, Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say: Due to suckling, you should consider unlawful those things which are considered unlawful due to lineage."
"5800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to him and said: O Anjasha! Drive gently, you are carrying glass vessels."
"5801","The Prophet ﷺ had a Had (a camel driver) called Anjasha, and he had a nice voice. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, ""(Drive) slowly, O Anjasha! Do not break the glass vessels!"" And Qatada said, ""(By vessels') he meant the weak women."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6211)"
"5802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Go gently, you are carrying glass vessels."
"5803","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was traveling, and with him was a black slave whose name was Anjasha. He was reciting poetry to urge the camels on. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""O Anjasha, go gently, you are carrying glass vessels."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) meant that he was carrying women."",""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ  was on a journey"",""and with him was a black servant named Anjasha. Anjasha was leading the way"","" so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ  said to him"","" 'O Anjasha"","" slow down and be gentle with your camel's cargo"","" meaning women.'"""""""
"5804","The narrator states) The narrator named Abdullah bin Buraidah used to perform two rak'ahs before Maghrib as well."
"5805","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In the blessed era of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), our food consisted of only two black things: dates and water."
"5806","The narrator states: Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) left from there and came to the mosque. He went to the gathering of the Ansar and related to them the entire incident that he had narrated to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and what Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had said to him. So they said, ""The youngest among us will go with you."" Thus, Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and went and testified to this. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""We did not accuse you of anything, but the matter of a hadith attributed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is important."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The command for the one seeking permission to return is in the case when the condition exists, and that is that permission is not obligatory. But when the condition is found, and that is granting permission, then the command to return will be considered nullified."
"5807","The one who is youngest among us will testify for you regarding this, and he is Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him)."" So Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) took Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) with him, and he testified before Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding this matter (that it is so). Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""This command of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained hidden from me; buying and selling in the market kept me unaware of it. However, accept whatever you wish (or greet as you wish)."
"5808","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Who is it?"" I replied, ""It is me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said twice, ""It is me, it is me,"" as if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked this."
"5809","I had known that you were peeping like this, I would have poked this comb into your eye. Permission to enter has been ordained so that (the household) may not be seen."
"5810","We were in the company of Ubayy b. Ka'b that Abu Musa Ash'ari came there in a state of anger. He stood (before us) and said: I ask you to bear witness in the name of Allah whether anyone amongst you heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Permission (for entering the house) should be sought three times and if permission is granted to you (then get in). otherwise go back. Ubayy b. Ka'b said: What is the iiiatter? He said: I sought permission yesterday from 'Umar b. Khattab three times but he did not permit me, so I came back; then I went to him today and visited him and informed him that I had come to him yesterday and greeted him thrice, then came back, whereupon he said: Yes, we did hear you but be were at that time busy, but why did you not seek permission (further and you must have never gone back until you were permitted to do so). He said: I sought permission (in the manner) that I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ having said (in connection 'With the seeking of permission for entering the house of a stranger). Thereupon he (Hadrat Umar) said: By Allah, I shall torture your back and your stomach unless you bring one who may bear witness to what you state. 'Ubayy b. Ka'b said: By Allah, none should stand with you (to bear testimony) but the youngest amongst us. And he therefore, said to Abu Sa'id: Stand up. So I stood up until I came to Umar and said: I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this. (Using translation from Muslim 2153c)"
"5811","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a person sends a messenger to another person, it will be considered as permission from him."
"5812","""Call yourselves by my name but do not call yourselves by my Kunyah."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3736)"
"5813","I did not call you, I called so-and-so.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Name yourselves after my name, but do not take my kunyah.”"
"5814","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Do not combine my name and my kunyah."
"5815","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that anyone should combine his name and his kunyah, and name someone Abu al-Qasim Muhammad."
"5816","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you adopt a kunyah, do not use my name, and when you use my name, do not adopt my kunyah."
"5817","I am Abu al-Qasim. Allah gives, and I distribute."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration has been heard by Ibn ‘Ajlan from Makbari and from his father, both. Both narrators are trustworthy, and both chains of this narration are preserved."
"5818","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""On the Day of Resurrection, you will be called by your names and the names of your fathers, so keep good names for yourselves.\"""""
"5819","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) changed the name of a woman from Asiyah. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You are"
"5820","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to a woman named ‘Asiyah: “You are Jameelah (beautiful).” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not do this because he intended a bad omen from the name ‘Asiyah, rather he wanted to take a good omen from the word Jameelah, and the same ruling applies to other such names. For the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has prohibited taking bad omens, as mentioned in another narration. S"
"5821","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) passed by a land whose name was ""Ghadrah,"" so he (peace be upon him) changed its name to ""Khudrah"" (meaning green and lush)."
"5822","I do not wish to change the name that my father gave me."" Saeed bin Musayyib says: After that, he always remained sorrowful."
"5823","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) heard a person saying: O Shahab! So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You are Hisham."
"5824","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Bad omens occur according to destiny. However, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) liked good omens."
"5825","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to take good omens and he (peace be upon him) liked to give good names."
"5826","“The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘There is no ‘Adwa* and no omen, but I like Al-Fa’l As-Salih.”** (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3537)"
